      "writtenOn": "2023-09-07T08:55:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It tends to be confusing to post() something on the same handler that is processing messages. In this case, the synchronous state machine is \"synchronous\" and that\u0027s its entire raison d\u0027être, so using its handler to post something for later doesn\u0027t sound like a good idea.\n\nI think that instead, we wanted to guarantee that there is never a mutual call that may end up in an infinite loop. Because the main state machine is asynchronous, could you instead make a message that will trigger this and break the loop ?",
